Write the Iceberg manifest key-value metadata the spec requires.

Against pg_lake v3.5.3. The Iceberg spec ("Manifests") says a manifest file
must store the partition spec and other metadata in its Avro key-value
metadata; for format v2 the keys schema, schema-id, partition-spec,
partition-spec-id, format-version and content are all required. pg_lake
writes only avro.schema and avro.codec, so spec-following readers reject its
manifests -- ClickHouse fails with "No partition-spec in iceberg manifest
file". Manifest lists are unaffected: the spec requires no keys there.

- avro.patch: write_header() also writes an optional "properties"
  map<string> of the extra-metadata record, so the header has 2 + N entries.
- avro_writer.c: AvroWriterCreateWithJsonSchemaAndProperties() takes a list
  of AvroMetadataProperty key/values and fills that map.
- write_manifest.c: WriteIcebergManifest() takes the schema, partition spec
  and content type and renders the six keys, reusing the metadata.json
  writers (AppendIcebergTableSchema is split out of AppendIcebergTableSchemas).
- metadata_operations.c: CreateManifestWriteContext() resolves the new
  snapshot's schema and all partition specs once per commit (including
  the ones a writable REST catalog table only has in the builder), and it is
  passed down to every UploadIcebergManifestToURI() call site, which already
  know the manifest's partition spec id and content type.

